WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.696 --> 00:00:07.843
The board shows every card of a project, in the stages of its workflow. Cards move by themselves as your agents work.

2
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:15.121
Open Board in the sidebar. Each column is a stage of the workflow, from Spec on the left to Done on the right.

3
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:23.265
The header counts the open and blocked cards and shows what the project spent this month. Each card shows what it has cost so far.

4
00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:29.173
The chips narrow the board. Blocked shows only the cards that wait for your answer at the desk.

5
00:00:29.872 --> 00:00:37.104
Waiting for my approval shows the cards you must approve. Waiting for my QA shows the ones you test before they are done.

6
00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:45.814
Click a card to open it. This one is blocked: its builder asked a question, and the card waits for your answer.

7
00:00:46.514 --> 00:00:53.810
The brief says what to build: context, requirements and acceptance criteria. The details show its stage and risk.

8
00:00:54.509 --> 00:01:03.170
Further down, the thread holds the conversation, with the question itself, and the handoffs record every shift: which agent did it, and the outcome.

9
00:01:03.874 --> 00:01:10.338
New card opens the form: a title, the repository and the brief. Cancel takes you back to the board.

10
00:01:11.225 --> 00:01:17.881
Pause project stops new work from starting. Running shifts finish, and Resume project picks up where it left off.

11
00:01:20.276 --> 00:01:26.527
Finished cards leave the board a day later. Archive lists them, and you can open or reopen any of them.

12
00:01:27.225 --> 00:01:32.516
That is the board. Check the chips each day, and open a card whenever you want the full story.
